Given the following text and a relational triplet extracted from it:

Text: You should not take this medicine if you are allergic to simvastatin, or if:
- you have active liver disease; or
- you are pregnant or breastfeeding.
The following drugs can increase your risk of serious muscle problems if you take them together with simvastatin. These drugs should not be used while you are taking this medicine:
- cyclosporine;
- danazol;
- gemfibrozil;
- nefazodone;
- an antibiotic - clarithromycin, erythromycin, telithromycin;
- antifungal medication - itraconazole, ketoconazole, posaconazole, voriconazole;
- hepatitis C medications - boceprevir, telaprevir; or
- HIV/AIDS medication - atazanavir, cobicistat (Stribild, Tybost), darunavir, fosamprenavir, indinavir, nelfinavir, ritonavir, saquinavir, tipranavir.
Before you start taking simvastatin, tell your doctor if you are already using any of these other medicines:
- lomitapide; or
- heart medication - amiodarone, amlodipine, diltiazem, dronedarone, ranolazine, verapamil.
To make sure simvastatin is safe for you, tell your doctor if you have:
- history of liver disease;
- history of kidney disease;
- diabetes;
Triplet: ["Simvastatin", "has contraindication", "use with clarithromycin"]

The relation 'has contraindication' in the triplet is defined as 'The subject drug should not be used in combination with the substance or medication specified by the object entity.' In this context, is there any relation appropriate to replace it? Choose a relation whose meaning and subject/object direction match the triplet even if the wording differs; choose 'None of the above' only if no candidate fits. Please answer by providing only the letter of your choice.

Choices:
A. 'contraindicated in': The subject drug should not be used by patients who have the condition or characteristic specified by the object entity.
B. 'should not be used in place of': The subject drug should not replace or substitute the treatment specified by the object entity.
C. 'should be avoided with': Patients taking the subject drug should avoid the substance or activity specified by the object entity.
D. 'not chemically related to': The subject drug does not share a chemical structure or mechanism of action with the substance specified by the object entity.
E. 'not used for': The subject drug is not indicated or used to treat the condition or situation specified by the object entity.
F. None of the above.

Answer:
